      "interpretation": {
        "what_this_is": "This project's reading of how the printed table's columns line up, not a rule the page states.",
        "row_alignment": "The rulebook prints each weapons table as four columns - type, class, Weapon Bonus, features - and the extractor reads it as two blocks: the names beside their class, and the bonuses beside their features. Pairing the two blocks row by row is this project's reading of the page, not something the page states. Three rows are printed a second time in prose and anchor it: p.87 gives the pistol two dice, p.87 gives the battle axe three, and Ch.4 p.80 gives the basic sword two."
